course: dictionary
lesson: 3374
title: One word, many meanings: exercise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and exercise is a good example. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air» tells you that an exercise book is something you write in, so here it means a school notebook.
explain: «Muscles grow stronger with use; astronauts in space lose muscle without gravity, so they exercise about two hours a day.» The clues are muscles and the body. Here exercise means moving the body to keep fit and healthy.
explain: «A physiotherapist gives exercises to bend and strengthen the arm.» Here an exercise is a set movement done to get stronger. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Exercise can be a noun (a thing or activity) or a verb (an action word, as in «to exercise»).
fact: Exercise means moving your body to keep fit and healthy, like running, swimming or playing sport.
fact: An exercise is a movement done to get stronger, or a piece of school work for practice.
fact: An exercise book is a notebook for school work.
fact: Children need about an hour of active play a day, and it is a good idea to warm up before exercise and drink water.
exercise: «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air.» What is an exercise book? | A book about sport | *A notebook for school work | A type of ball | A book of very hard jokes
exercise: «Astronauts in space exercise about two hours a day.» What does exercise mean here? | Writing answers in a notebook | Sitting still and resting | Playing a card game | *Moving the body to keep fit and healthy
exercise: In maths, Priya is given an exercise to do at home. What is an exercise here? | A type of sport shoe | A loud noise | *A set of questions for practice | A kind of food
test: «A pet needs food, water, care and exercise every day.» What does exercise mean here? | A school notebook | A set of maths questions | *Physical activity to keep the pet fit | Lying still in its bed
test: Which word means a movement done to get stronger, as in «stretching exercises»? | physiotherapist | *exercise | notebook | pet
exam: «Warm up before you exercise and drink water.» In this sentence, what does to exercise mean? | To write neatly in a notebook | To answer a set of questions | To fall asleep | *To do physical activity
